QEMU, AND OUR CHANGE TO IT

The drive edition carries a Windows QEMU binary we built, with one patch of
our own to QEMU's block/file-win32.c. QEMU is GPL-2.0; a derivative of
GPL-2.0 code is GPL-2.0 whoever wrote it, and so is the recipe that
compiles it. So launcher/qemu-windows/win32-hdev-fixed-length.patch and
launcher/qemu-windows/keephaven-qemu.nix are GPL-2.0-only, cannot be
relicensed by anyone, and are not offered under other terms. Every drive
carries QEMU's own licence, the patch in full, the build recipe, the
package pin, and a written offer of the complete corresponding source good
for three years.

